-- title:
--   Retraction and local parameter along a section of a smooth relative curve
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a local commutative ring, let $X$ be a scheme and let $c \colon X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a morphism that is smooth of relative dimension $1$. Let $\sigma \colon \operatorname{Spec} R \to X$ be a section of $c$, i.e. $\sigma$ followed by $c$ is the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} R$, and let $s$ be a point of the underlying space of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ whose singleton $\{s\}$ is closed. Write $S = \mathcal{O}_{X, \sigma(s)}$ for the stalk of the structure sheaf of $X$ at the image point $\sigma(s)$, regarded as an $R$-algebra through the ring map $R \cong \Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} R, \mathcal{O}) \to \Gamma(X, \mathcal{O}_X) \to S$ obtained from the canonical isomorphism $\Gamma \circ \operatorname{Spec} \cong \mathrm{id}$, the map induced by $c$ on global sections, and the germ map at $\sigma(s)$. The assertion is that there exist an $R$-algebra homomorphism $\pi \colon S \to R$ and an element $t \in S$ such that: the kernel of the stalk map $S \to \mathcal{O}_{\operatorname{Spec} R, s}$ induced by $\sigma$ is contained in $\ker \pi$; $\pi(t) = 0$; $\ker \pi \subseteq (t) + (\ker \pi)^2$ as ideals of $S$; and the module of Kähler differentials $\Omega_{S/R}$ is a finite $S$-module.
--
--   This packages, at the stalk of a smooth relative curve at a point of a section over a local base, the standard facts that a section of a smooth morphism is a regular immersion whose conormal module is invertible in relative dimension one (so its ideal is generated by one element modulo its square), that evaluation along the section gives an $R$-algebra retraction, and that the sheaf of relative differentials is locally free of rank one. It is used to produce a local parameter at a cusp and a retraction of the stalk, feeding the identification of the kernel of the stalk map as a principal ideal and the power-series expansion arguments on modular curve models.
